excerpt: >-
  Everything I could ask for in a horror film.
---

Everything I could ask for in a horror film.

From a technical perspective, immersive atmosphere, incredible cinematography, powerful symbolism and a chilling score behind it all. Child actors did phenomenal, specifically Caleb's.

From a film perspective, the gradual build up keeps an unnerving feeling throughout the film, ending in an extremely haunting and powerful final 10 minutes. And we are still left wondering what the source of the evil really is. Not only from the obvious, but also because the family depicts pride, lust, envy, sloth, and in the end, wrath. Highlights the dangers of obsessive piety and is a great exploration of human psychology under stress.

Great film.
